  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="r5-status-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">AVOCADOMINI R5 / STATUS AS OF 21 OCT 2026</p><h1>In design.<br /><em>Not yet for sale.</em></h1><p class="lead">The slender, detachable Mini is a product direction. One self-contained unit has not passed the physical, software, and connectivity tests needed for release.</p><div class="r5-closed" role="status">NO RESERVATION · NO PAYMENT · PRICE NOT SET</div></div><figure><img src="/images/avocadomini-r5-slim-home-concept.png" alt="Concept visualization of a slim silver avocadoMini with a black sensor band in a home" /><figcaption>Concept visualization; not a production device or an accepted call interface.</figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="r5-status-details" aria-labelledby="r5-details-title"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT EXISTS / WHAT IS STILL OPEN</p><h2 id="r5-details-title">The work is visible.<br />The gates are open.</h2><div class="r5-status-grid"><article><span>01 / REQUIREMENTS</span><strong>Documented</strong><p>The intended one-unit, ≤ 200 mm design and home-to-portable experience have a written baseline.</p></article><article><span>02 / PHYSICAL PROTOTYPE</span><strong>Not accepted</strong><p>One closed device has not passed display, input, identity, power, heat, calls, optional LTE/IoT data SIM, and Wi-Fi sharing together.</p></article><article><span>03 / MINI SOFTWARE</span><strong>Not accepted</strong><p>RockstarOS, Sky, and Zema still need a signed Mini build, device-specific permissions, persistence, and recovery evidence.</p></article><article><span>04 / COMMERCIAL RELEASE</span><strong>Closed</strong><p>Price, sale region, release date, delivery, and support terms remain undecided. Checkout and reservations stay closed.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="r5-next" aria-labelledby="r5-next-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">NEXT MILESTONES</p><h2 id="r5-next-title">Prove one Mini<br />before promising many.</h2></div><ol><li>Compare the optical, radio, battery, and thermal envelope on real components.</li><li>Build one closed prototype and measure the spatial input, display, call, and portable network path.</li><li>Accept the same device through OS permissions, stop, update, restart, and recovery.</li><li>Set the final specification, price, service conditions, and release plan only from accepted evidence.</li></ol></section>
    <section class="r5-status-bottom"><p>Older Tower20 E3 images and prices are historical design studies. They are not the current R5 product configuration or an R5 offer.</p><div><a class="button" href="https://avocadomini.si/">Explore the R5 concept ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/install/">Use the available Web preview ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/legal/">Read sales disclosure ↗</a></div></section>
